#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""claude-sessions: Claude Code session status in the GNOME top bar.

Subcommands:
  claude-sessions [indicator]   start the top bar indicator (AppIndicator)
  claude-sessions hook          entry point for Claude Code hooks (JSON on stdin)
  claude-sessions status        list sessions in the terminal
  claude-sessions clean         delete state files whose PID is gone
  claude-sessions setup         register the hooks in ~/.claude/settings.json
  claude-sessions unsetup       remove those hooks again
  claude-sessions --version     print the version

One file per session in ~/.local/state/claude-sessions/<session_id>.json.
GTK imports are lazy: the `hook` subcommand only uses the stdlib so it starts
in ~30 ms.
"""

